By a logical matrix we mean a triple $ \langle V,C,D\rangle $, where $ V $ is the set of truth values, $ C $ is the set of functions corresponding to connectives, and $ D $ is the set of designated values. The entailment relation is defined as follows:
\begin{center}
$\Gamma\models\Delta$ iff, for every valuation $v$, if
$v(A)\in D$ for every $A\in\Gamma$, then $v(B)\in D$ for some
$B\in\Delta$. 
\end{center}

For every finite multiset of formulas $\Gamma$ and every formula $A$, the following hold:
 \begin{itemize}
     \item $\Gamma \models_{\bf K_3^d} A$ iff $ \vdash_{\bf K_3^d} \Gamma \Rightarrow A \mid \;\Rightarrow$,
     \item $\Gamma \models_{\bf LP^d} A$ iff $ \vdash_{\bf LP^d} \;\Rightarrow\; \mid \Gamma \Rightarrow A $.
 \end{itemize}

The following cut rules are admissible in \textbf{BSC}:
\begin{center}
	$(Cut\mid)$ \ $\dfrac{\Gamma 
	\Rightarrow  \Delta, A \mid \Lambda\Rightarrow\Theta \qquad
	A, \Pi  \Rightarrow  \Sigma \mid \Xi\Rightarrow\Omega} {\Gamma, \Pi  \Rightarrow  \Delta, \Sigma \mid \Lambda, \Xi\Rightarrow\Theta, \Omega}$
\end{center}

\begin{center}
	$(\mid Cut)$ \ $\dfrac{\Gamma 
	\Rightarrow  \Delta \mid \Lambda\Rightarrow\Theta, A \qquad
	\Pi  \Rightarrow  \Sigma \mid A, \Xi\Rightarrow\Omega} {\Gamma, \Pi  \Rightarrow  \Delta, \Sigma \mid \Lambda, \Xi\Rightarrow\Theta, \Omega}$
\end{center}
